# Phase gate rules (V12–V13, V19)

## V12 — HTTP push (Phase 2)

Do not wire `RestTemplate.postForObject` (or similar) to `metrics.api.endpoint` without:
1. Phase 1 exit criteria confirmed
2. Explicit user approval to enter Phase 2
3. ADR for push semantics (retry, failure handling)

`RestTemplate` bean may exist; HTTP send is deferred until Phase 2 gate.

## V13 — Actuator exposure (Phase 4)

Do not expose Actuator endpoints (`management.endpoints.web.exposure.include`) without:
1. Phase 3 complete (dashboard UI) or explicitly waived by user
2. Explicit user approval to enter Phase 4
3. Security review documented

Actuator dependency on classpath is allowed; endpoint exposure is phase-gated.

## V19 — Dashboard UI (Phase 3)

Do not add `MetricsController`, static dashboard, or SSE endpoints without:
1. Phase 1 exit criteria confirmed
2. Explicit user approval to enter Phase 3
3. ADR-003 accepted (`docs/DECISIONS/ADR-003-metrics-dashboard.md`)

Follow `docs/UI_PLAN.md` for API and screen design. UI must use `MetricsSnapshotStore` (V16), not log parsing.

## General

See `docs/PHASE_GATES.md` for full phase definitions. Ask user before starting Phase N+1 work.
